;; negation over lattice keys (docs/incremental.md 0.8): ~(best X) takes
;; the KEY columns only and means "no value at key X" -- an absence probe
;; of the closed lattice relation's payload map.
lattice (low (min int))
table (best int low)
table (k int)
table (nobest int)

rule
(best 1 10) (best 1 5) (best 2 7)
(k 1) (k 2) (k 3)

rule
(k X)
~(best X)
-->
(nobest X)
